# Line-ending policy
# =============================================================================
# CGPU is developed on both Windows and Linux/macOS, but almost everything it produces RUNS
# on Linux: the k3s nodes, the containers, the shell scripts, the guard.
#
# Without this file, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true checks shell scripts out with
# CRLF endings, and every one of them then fails on a Linux node with:
#
#     env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# That is not a hypothetical - it silently broke three of the A3 GPU e2e tests, which looked
# like a regression in the code under test rather than a checkout artefact. Pinning LF here
# makes the checkout correct regardless of each developer's local git settings.

# Default: normalise to LF in the repository and check out LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Things that must be LF because Linux executes or parses them directly.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
*.c     text eol=lf
*.h     text eol=lf
*.cu    text eol=lf
*.go    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
*.mod   text eol=lf
*.sum   text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts, which genuinely want CRLF.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf

# Never touched.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.so    binary
*.vhdx  binary
